{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778977431841,"sessionID":"ses_1ccb09deeffeCm27z5qRSqxwBn","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_lpvixzNRt9qFqXGjYuW14JMR","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/__w/eval-ont-agent-cl/eval-ont-agent-cl/src/ontology/cl-edit.owl","offset":34426,"limit":32},"output":"<path>/__w/eval-ont-agent-cl/eval-ont-agent-cl/src/ontology/cl-edit.owl</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n34426: SubClassOf(obo:CL_4070017 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002162 obo:NCBITaxon_6657))\n34427: \n34428: # Class: obo:CL_4072001 (newly formed oligodendrocyte)\n34429: \n34430: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:27284195\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:39233334\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4072001 \"A post-mitotic oligodendrocyte that has exited the cell cycle and begun early stage differentiation. The cell begins to acquire oligodendrocyte-like characteristics but has not yet initiated myelination. In mice, NFOL is marked by the expression of Tcf7l2 and Cemip2 (also known as Tmem2), among other early myelin-related genes. These markers highlight cells transitioning from a precursor to a more differentiated, pre-myelinating state.\")\n34431: AnnotationAssertion(terms:contributor obo:CL_4072001 <https://orcid.org/0000-0002-5507-2103>)\n34432: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:27284195\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType obo:OMO_0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym obo:CL_4072001 \"NFOL\")\n34433: AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_4072001 \"newly formed oligodendrocyte\"@en)\n34434: SubClassOf(obo:CL_4072001 obo:CL_0000123)\n34435: SubClassOf(obo:CL_4072001 obo:CL_0000128)\n34436: SubClassOf(obo:CL_4072001 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:BFO_0000050 obo:UBERON_0001017))\n34437: SubClassOf(obo:CL_4072001 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002207 obo:CL_4023059))\n34438: \n34439: # Class: obo:CL_4072002 (myelin-forming oligodendrocyte)\n34440: \n34441: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:27284195\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:30837646\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:39233334\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:9473608\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4072002 \"A postmitotic and differentiated oligodendrocyte derived from a oligodendrocyte progenitor cell. A myelin-forming oligodendrocyte begins the expression of myelin genes and actively engages in the myelination process. In mice and humans, it is characterized by the upregulation of the key myelin-associated markers Mbp and Opalin. Additionally, Ctps (CTP synthase) shows peak expression at this stage, suggesting a heightened demand for nucleotide biosynthesis during membrane expansion and myelin production.\")\n34442: AnnotationAssertion(terms:contributor obo:CL_4072002 <https://orcid.org/0000-0002-5507-2103>)\n34443: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:39233334\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType obo:OMO_0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym obo:CL_4072002 \"MFOL\")\n34444: AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_4072002 \"myelin-forming oligodendrocyte\"@en)\n34445: SubClassOf(obo:CL_4072002 obo:CL_0000128)\n34446: SubClassOf(obo:CL_4072002 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:BFO_0000050 obo:UBERON_0001017))\n34447: SubClassOf(obo:CL_4072002 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002207 obo:CL_4072001))\n34448: SubClassOf(obo:CL_4072002 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002215 obo:GO_0032289))\n34449: \n34450: # Class: obo:CL_4072003 (mature myelinating oligodendrocyte)\n34451: \n34452: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:27284195\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:33203872\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4072003 \"A post-mitotic oligodendrocyte derived from a myelin-forming oligodendrocyte (MFOL). A mature Myelinating Oligodendrocyte is a fully differentiated cell that is actively engaged in myelination. In addition to high expression of canonical myelin genes (e.g., Mbp, Plp1, Mog), a MOL can be distinguished by the expression of stage-enriched genes Grm3, Klk6, Ptgds, Anxa5, and Hopx in mice. These markers reflect the functional specialization of a mature oligodendrocyte, including roles in signalling, lipid metabolism, and myelin maintenance.\")\n34453: AnnotationAssertion(terms:contributor obo:CL_4072003 <https://orcid.org/0000-0002-5507-2103>)\n34454: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:27284195\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType obo:OMO_0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym obo:CL_4072003 \"MOL\")\n34455: AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_4072003 \"mature myelinating oligodendrocyte\")\n34456: SubClassOf(obo:CL_4072003 obo:CL_0000128)\n34457: SubClassOf(obo:CL_4072003 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:BFO_0000051 obo:GO_0043209))\n\n(Showing lines 34426-34457 of 34709. Use offset=34458 to continue.)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"SubClassOf(obo:CL_4070017 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002162 obo:NCBITaxon_6657))\n\n# Class: obo:CL_4072001 (newly formed oligodendrocyte)\n\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:27284195\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:39233334\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4072001 \"A post-mitotic oligodendrocyte that has exited the cell cycle and begun early stage differentiation. The cell begins to acquire oligodendrocyte-like characteristics but has not yet initiated myelination. In mice, NFOL is marked by the expression of Tcf7l2 and Cemip2 (also known as Tmem2), among other early myelin-related genes. These markers highlight cells transitioning from a precursor to a more differentiated, pre-myelinating state.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(terms:contributor obo:CL_4072001 <https://orcid.org/0000-0002-5507-2103>)\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:27284195\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType obo:OMO_0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym obo:CL_4072001 \"NFOL\")\nAnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_4072001 \"newly formed oligodendrocyte\"@en)\nSubClassOf(obo:CL_4072001 obo:CL_0000123)\nSubClassOf(obo:CL_4072001 obo:CL_0000128)\nSubClassOf(obo:CL_4072001 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:BFO_0000050 obo:UBERON_0001017))\nSubClassOf(obo:CL_4072001 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002207 obo:CL_4023059))\n\n# Class: obo:CL_4072002 (myelin-forming oligodendrocyte)\n\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:27284195\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:30837646\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:39233334\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:9473608\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4072002 \"A postmitotic and differentiated oligodendrocyte derived from a oligodendrocyte progenitor cell. A myelin-forming oligodendrocyte begins the expression of myelin genes and actively engages in the myelination process. In mice and humans, it is characterized by the upregulation of the key myelin-associated markers Mbp and Opalin. Additionally, Ctps (CTP synthase) shows peak expression at this stage, suggesting a heightened demand for nucleotide biosynthesis during membrane expansion and myelin production.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(terms:contributor obo:CL_4072002 <https://orcid.org/0000-0002-5507-2103>)\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:39233334\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType obo:OMO_0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym obo:CL_4072002 \"MFOL\")\nAnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_4072002 \"myelin-forming oligodendrocyte\"@en)\nSubClassOf(obo:CL_4072002 obo:CL_0000128)","truncated":true,"loaded":[]},"title":"src/ontology/cl-edit.owl","time":{"start":1778977431714,"end":1778977431839}},"id":"prt_e3351609d001ppqdW7UOMIqVq8","sessionID":"ses_1ccb09deeffeCm27z5qRSqxwBn","messageID":"msg_e335142d50016ctQOfOIPMahEv"}}
