{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778977526812,"sessionID":"ses_1ccb09deeffeCm27z5qRSqxwBn","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"apply_patch","callID":"call_LovJt8BpwLCtUJ2EAvZHuKd7","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"patchText":"*** Begin Patch\n*** Add File: /__w/eval-ont-agent-cl/eval-ont-agent-cl/ISSUE_COMMENTS.md\n+Addressed in PR #<NN>.\n+\n+Added a new `quiescent fibroblast` term as a subclass of `fibroblast`, with the requested synonym and literature-backed definition.\n*** Add File: /__w/eval-ont-agent-cl/eval-ont-agent-cl/PR_COMMENTS.md\n+Added a new CL term for `quiescent fibroblast` in `src/ontology/cl-edit.owl`.\n+\n+What changed:\n+- Added new class `CL_4072103` with label `quiescent fibroblast`.\n+- Added a textual definition supported by `PMID:21049082`, `PMID:35701396`, `PMID:40538750`, and `doi:10.1038/s41427-020-0226-7`.\n+- Added the exact synonym `inactive fibroblast` with `PMID:22529592`.\n+- Placed the new term under `fibroblast` (`CL_0000057`).\n+- Added standard new-term metadata: issue tracker link, creation date, and creator annotation.\n+\n+Rationale:\n+- The issue requested a distinct term for the quiescent state of fibroblasts.\n+- The definition text and comments in the issue describe a stable fibroblast state distinct from activated myofibroblast states, so a named subclass of `fibroblast` was appropriate.\n+- I kept the logical modeling minimal because there was no established quiescence pattern for fibroblast state terms in the surrounding ontology content.\n+\n+Checks completed:\n+- Confirmed the requested label and synonym were not already present in `src/ontology/cl-edit.owl`.\n+- Checked the existing `fibroblast` term and recent new-term blocks to match local annotation style.\n+- Reviewed the git diff to ensure only the intended ontology changes were included in the commit.\n+\n+Validation:\n+- Performed structural validation by checking the new declaration, class stanza, references, and subclass placement in `cl-edit.owl`.\n+- Did not run a full ontology reasoner or ROBOT validation command in this pass.\n*** End Patch"},"output":"Success. Updated the following files:\nA ISSUE_COMMENTS.md\nA PR_COMMENTS.md","metadata":{"diff":"Index: /__w/eval-ont-agent-cl/eval-ont-agent-cl/ISSUE_COMMENTS.md\n===================================================================\n--- /__w/eval-ont-agent-cl/eval-ont-agent-cl/ISSUE_COMMENTS.md\n+++ /__w/eval-ont-agent-cl/eval-ont-agent-cl/ISSUE_COMMENTS.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,3 @@\n+Addressed in PR #<NN>.\n+\n+Added a new `quiescent fibroblast` term as a subclass of `fibroblast`, with the requested synonym and literature-backed definition.\n\nIndex: /__w/eval-ont-agent-cl/eval-ont-agent-cl/PR_COMMENTS.md\n===================================================================\n--- /__w/eval-ont-agent-cl/eval-ont-agent-cl/PR_COMMENTS.md\n+++ /__w/eval-ont-agent-cl/eval-ont-agent-cl/PR_COMMENTS.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,22 @@\n+Added a new CL term for `quiescent fibroblast` in `src/ontology/cl-edit.owl`.\n+\n+What changed:\n+- Added new class `CL_4072103` with label `quiescent fibroblast`.\n+- Added a textual definition supported by `PMID:21049082`, `PMID:35701396`, `PMID:40538750`, and `doi:10.1038/s41427-020-0226-7`.\n+- Added the exact synonym `inactive fibroblast` with `PMID:22529592`.\n+- Placed the new term under `fibroblast` (`CL_0000057`).\n+- Added standard new-term metadata: issue tracker link, creation date, and creator annotation.\n+\n+Rationale:\n+- The issue requested a distinct term for the quiescent state of fibroblasts.\n+- The definition text and comments in the issue describe a stable fibroblast state distinct from activated myofibroblast states, so a named subclass of `fibroblast` was appropriate.\n+- I kept the logical modeling minimal because there was no established quiescence pattern for fibroblast state terms in the surrounding ontology content.\n+\n+Checks completed:\n+- Confirmed the requested label and synonym were not already present in `src/ontology/cl-edit.